      "fields": {
        "definition": "Instantiation of the source's universal statement: for the single modeled duplicated chromosome (one sister-chromatid pair), during metaphase it is aligned at the metaphase plate (equatorial plane) midway between the two poles. The relation holds for this instance only; it does not assert universal quantification across all chromosomes.",
